From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:01:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito/sargo: drop the includes lineage-24.0 no longer has

This device tree is 22.2 and the platform is 24.0, so three includes point at files that no longer
exist and product config stops before lunch:

- hardware/google/pixel/vibrator/drv2624 -- the whole vibrator/ directory is gone from that repo on
  24.0. drv2624 is the Pixel 3a's 2018 haptic driver.
- hardware/google/pixel/PixelLogger -- gone from the same repo. A logging tool, not a HAL.
- device/google/gs-common/thermal/thermal_hal -- gs-common's thermal/ is empty at the pinned branch.

Commented rather than deleted, with the reason, because these are things to restore rather than
things that were wrong: the vibrator HAL can be vendored from the 22.2 tree, and thermal wants a
gs-common pin that still carries it. The first question is whether a 22.2 device tree configures and
compiles against Android 17 at all, and none of these affects that.

The one other missing include, vendor/google_devices/bonito/proprietary/BoardConfigVendor.mk, is a
`-include` and absent on 22.2 as well -- it has never been there and does not fail.
---
 device.mk | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device.mk b/device.mk
index 4d697a25..4b40ab46 100644
--- a/device.mk
+++ b/device.mk
@@ -719,9 +719,13 @@ PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
 PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES += ro.soc.manufacturer=Qualcomm
 PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES += ro.soc.model=SDM670
 
-include hardware/google/pixel/vibrator/drv2624/device.mk
+# lineage-24.0: hardware/google/pixel dropped vibrator/ entirely; drv2624 is a 2018 part and the
+# HAL went with it. No haptics until it is vendored back from the 22.2 tree, which still has it.
+#include hardware/google/pixel/vibrator/drv2624/device.mk
 include hardware/google/pixel/mm/device_legacy.mk
-include device/google/gs-common/thermal/thermal_hal/device.mk
+# lineage-24.0: gs-common's thermal/ is empty at the branch this device pins, so there is no
+# thermal_hal to include. Thermal falls back to whatever the blobs provide.
+#include device/google/gs-common/thermal/thermal_hal/device.mk
 
 # Citadel
 include hardware/google/pixel/citadel/citadel.mk
@@ -730,4 +734,6 @@ include hardware/google/pixel/citadel/citadel.mk
 -include hardware/google/pixel/power-libperfmgr/aidl/device.mk
 
 # Pixel Logger
-include hardware/google/pixel/PixelLogger/PixelLogger.mk
+# lineage-24.0: PixelLogger is gone from hardware/google/pixel too. A logging tool, not a HAL --
+# nothing depends on it to boot.
+#include hardware/google/pixel/PixelLogger/PixelLogger.mk
-- 
2.53.0

